      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Contributor/maintainer action is needed because automation cannot supply the contributor's real MiniMax/OpenClaw runtime proof for them.; Cleared: The diff only touches MiniMax provider parse handling, tests, and a proof script; it adds no dependency, workflow, lockfile, secret, permission, or downloaded-code execution surface. (sha=abd3291e748b3644bacd12d9bfea3eecd19fcfc4)",
      "review_summary": "The PR wraps MiniMax music stream-frame JSON parsing, skips malformed SSE frames in `readStreamingTrack`, adds a mocked regression test, and adds a standalone parser proof script.\n\nPR surface: Source +13, Tests +137. Total +150 across 3 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. by source inspection: current main routes non-empty MiniMax music SSE `data:` frames through a bare `JSON.parse`, so malformed JSON can throw before later valid audio frames are processed. I did not run a live malformed MiniMax stream in this read-only review.",
