      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(minimax): guard music generation SSE JSON.parse against malformed frames",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/minimax/music-generation-provider.ts:266` calls `JSON.parse(json)` on SSE data frames without try/catch. A malformed SSE data frame → unhandled `SyntaxError` → music generation crashes instead of skipping the bad frame.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/minimax/music-generation-provider.ts`: extract `parseMinimaxMusicStreamFrame()` helper that wraps `JSON.parse` with try/catch → throws descriptive `Error(\"MiniMax music generation returned malformed SSE JSON frame.\")` instead of raw `SyntaxError`. Call site in `readStreamingTrack()` catches and `continue`s (skips bad frame), preserving existing behavior.\n- `extensions/minimax/music-generation-provider.test.ts`: two tests verifying the fix (mocked SSE + real HTTP server)\n- `test/_proof_minimax_music_json_guard.mts`: standalone proof script that imports and calls the actual `parseMinimaxMusicStreamFrame()` function directly\n\nThis follows the same pattern as merged D4 JSON.parse guard PRs: #97889 (discord), #97973 (matrix), #97999 (twilio), #98073 (signal), #98587 (slack).\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Standalone proof script (L2) — calls the ACTUAL exported function\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx test/_proof_minimax_music_json_guard.mts\n\n[1] malformed SSE frame JSON → descriptive Error\n  PASS  throws Error (not SyntaxError)\n  PASS  message includes \"malformed SSE JSON frame\"\n\n[2] valid MiniMax music frame → returns correctly\n  PASS  no error thrown\n  PASS  returns object\n  PASS  audio hex preserved\n  PASS  base_resp.status_code is 0\n\n[3] empty string → throws Error\n  PASS  throws Error for empty string\n\n[4] non-object JSON → parses (type check is caller's responsibility)\n  PASS  no error thrown for valid JSON string\n  PASS  returns the parsed string value\n\n==================================================\n  Passed: 9  Failed: 0  Total: 9\n==================================================\n```\n\nBefore (current main): `JSON.parse(\"NOT JSON {{{\")` → raw `SyntaxError` crashes music generation\nAfter (this PR): `parseMinimaxMusicStreamFrame(\"NOT JSON {{{\")` → descriptive `Error: MiniMax music generation returned malformed SSE JSON frame.`\n\n### Real HTTP server test (L2) — vitest + live node:http server\n\nThe test starts a real `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1:0`, serves an SSE stream with `data: NOT JSON {{{` followed by a valid MiniMax audio frame, then calls `generateMusic()` via `postJsonRequest` forwarded to the local server through real `fetch()`.\n\n```\n$ MINIMAX_API_KEY=test pnpm exec vitest run extensions/minimax/music-generation-provider.test.ts\n\n ✓ real HTTP server proof: malformed SSE frame → skip, valid audio → decoded\n ✓ skips malformed SSE data frames and processes valid audio frames\n ... (all existing tests pass)\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  15 passed (15)\n   Duration  48.70s\n```\n\n### Negative control (L3)\n\nStashing the try/catch and reverting to bare `JSON.parse(json)` causes the real-HTTP-server test to fail with unhandled `SyntaxError`, confirming the fix is real and the test is not a tautology.",
